1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,310
It's a touchy subject.
这是个敏感话题。

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:06,880
Talking socially about money can make people feel uncomfortable.
在社交场合谈论金钱会让人感到不自在。

3
00:00:06,880 --> 00:00:19,930
But at work, have a conversation about how much people earn, and things can not only get awkward, but, in some cases, it can get you sacked.
而在职场中，聊起收入这件事，不仅会让场面变得尴尬，在某些情况下，甚至还会让你丢了工作。

4
00:00:19,930 --> 00:00:30,360
According to a survey by the Trades Union Congress, 1 in 5 workers "have been told they can’t talk about their pay at work".
英国职工总会的一项调查显示，五分之一的员工“被告知不能在工作场合谈论自己的薪资”。

5
00:00:30,360 --> 00:00:38,770
This, concludes the TUC, indicates how common pay secrecy or 'gagging' clauses are in employment contracts.
职工总会称，这一数据表明薪资保密或“封口”条款在雇佣合同中十分普遍。

6
00:00:38,770 --> 00:00:47,570
'Pay secrecy clauses are a get out of jail free card for bad bosses,' said TUC general secretary Frances O'Grady.
职工总会秘书长弗朗西斯·奥格雷迪表示：“薪资保密条款是无良老板的‘免罪符’。

7
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:55,390
'They stop workers from challenging unfair pay, allow top executives to hoard profits and encourage discrimination.
这些条款阻止员工对不公平薪酬提出质疑，纵容高管隐藏收益，还会助长歧视现象。

8
00:00:55,390 --> 00:01:01,290
More openness about wages is essential to building fairer workplaces.'
薪资信息更加公开透明，对于打造更公平的职场环境至关重要。”

9
00:01:01,290 --> 00:01:04,940
So, should we talk about how much we earn?
那么，我们到底该不该谈论自己的收入呢？

10
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:06,710
It's not so simple.
事情并没有那么简单。

11
00:01:06,710 --> 00:01:11,640
Even without the contractual obligations, people may still be reluctant.
即便没有合同条款的约束，人们可能依然不愿提及此事。

12
00:01:11,640 --> 00:01:20,690
"I personally have found it's better not looking and not knowing," Tracy Jordan, an HR professional, told the BBC.
人力资源从业者特雷西·乔丹告诉BBC：“就我个人而言，我觉得眼不见为净。

13
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:28,750
"Even if you feel you are paid a fair wage, there will always be someone that you perceive is doing a lesser job and is earning more.
就算你觉得自己的薪水很公道，也总会发现有人干的活更少，拿的钱却更多。

14
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:35,580
Rather than feeling perpetually dissatisfied, I think ignorance can be bliss."
与其一直心怀不满，不如无知是福。”

15
00:01:35,580 --> 00:01:51,080
Money is tied up with complex emotions, Brianna McGurran, a money expert at the personal finance blog NerdWallet, told the New York Times. It involves emotions like shame, success and fear of failure.
个人理财博客“书呆子钱包”的理财专家布里安娜·麦古兰在接受《纽约时报》采访时表示，金钱往往与复杂的情绪挂钩，其中包含羞耻感、成就感以及对失败的恐惧。

16
00:01:51,080 --> 00:01:57,740
It also influences how people view you. People's money is tied to their self-worth.
金钱还会影响他人对你的看法，人们会将收入与自我价值绑定。

17
00:01:57,740 --> 00:02:03,340
As a result, culturally, it can be bit of a taboo.
因此，从文化层面来讲，谈论金钱算得上是一个禁忌话题。

18
00:02:03,340 --> 00:02:07,200
But all that may change.
但这一切或许都将改变。

19
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:15,690
First of all, pay secrecy clauses are unenforceable in the UK due to the UK Equality Act 2010.
首先，根据英国《2010年平等法案》，薪资保密条款在英国不具备法律效力。

20
00:02:15,690 --> 00:02:22,500
An employee must always be able to find out if they are being discriminated against in terms of pay.
员工有权查明自己是否遭遇了薪酬歧视。

21
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:32,290
In addition, The European Union is considering new legislation on pay transparency in order to reduce gender pay, earnings and pension gaps.
此外，欧盟正考虑出台有关薪资透明度的新法规，以缩小性别薪酬差距、收入差距以及养老金差距。

22
00:02:32,290 --> 00:02:38,080
So, for better or worse it may be something we all have to get used to.
所以，无论好坏，这都是我们所有人不得不去适应的趋势。

23
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:43,920
Over time, talking about our salaries may become just another matter for small talk.
假以时日，谈论薪资或许会成为日常闲聊中的又一个话题而已。
